# VERA 2026-09-24: operational artifacts + untracked binaries (CI builds graph from manifest; see 2026-09-21 handoff)
__pycache__/
knowledge/graph/graph.db
knowledge/graph/graph_index.json
knowledge/graph/sessions.db
reflection/stale/
reflection/trace/
reflection/events.jsonl
# Provenance ledger: the PostToolUse hook appends to it on every tool use
# (scripts/provenance_logger.py). Generated audit state like events.jsonl
# above, not source - committing it would leave the worktree permanently
# dirty. The chain is per-clone by design; \`verify\` checks it.
reflection/provenance_ledger.jsonl
# Per-candidate root-cause output written by pipeline/06_reflect/spawn.py and
# scripts/root_cause_attribution.py. An empty copy was tracked here and
# deleted 2026-09-28; a generated output dir does not belong in VCS.
reflection/diagnostics/
# Background-reflection supervisor runtime state (pipeline/06_reflect/background_worker.py):
#   {topic}.status.json  terminal state the worker must never fake (done|failed|timeout|error)
#   {topic}.lock         PID of the in-flight worker, for same-topic mutual exclusion
#   {topic}.log          agent stdout/stderr plus the gate's failure output
# All three are regenerable per-run telemetry. The digests/candidates a run
# PRODUCES are tracked separately and must never be deleted on failure - a
# gate-flagged artifact is the evidence (see CLAUDE.md tooling hygiene).
reflection/logs/
knowledge/raw_local/
# Every binary type ingest accepts. `*.pdf` alone was narrower than
# `scripts/ingest.py`, which takes .epub and .txt as well — so an ingested
# epub landed in knowledge/raw/ as untracked debris, which is exactly how the
# Agentforce source was deleted on 2026-09-21 (74b922e). Workspace `library/`
# is where binaries live; this project keeps a working copy only.
knowledge/raw/*.pdf
knowledge/raw/*.epub
knowledge/raw/*.txt
# knowledge/corpus/ is derived, not source: 10,337 chunk files projected from
# ~110 raw sources, a 21:1 ratio that puts a rebuildable projection in version
# control and makes the repo unreadable. Chunking is deterministic and
# byte-identical — verified by regenerating a source through INBOX/ and diffing
# against the committed chunk. Rebuild with `python scripts/ingest.py`.
# knowledge/raw/manifest.jsonl stays tracked: it is the reverse index
# (source -> chunk ids) a fresh clone needs to know what it is missing.
# Untracked 2026-09-28 per D5; see ADR-0003.
knowledge/corpus/

# operational archive (mirrors emptied INBOX; audit content, not lab knowledge)
INBOX_archive/

